Purpose 

This assignment assesses the learner’s ability to interpret NIST SP 800-53, translate a control into operating requirements, define an evidence request, identify unresolved matters, and maintain reference traceability. The assignment uses synthetic NovaPay information only. 

Learning Objectives 

Explain the role and limitations of NIST SP 800-53 in an organizational context. 

Interpret AC-2 Account Management and translate it into account-lifecycle requirements. 

Apply the interpretation to access governance for the NovaPay Transaction Platform. 

Prepare a complete and proportionate evidence request for a quarterly access review. 

Identify uncertainties and matters requiring clarification or escalation. 

Document the publication edition and references that informed the analysis. 

Simulation Context 

Item 

Description 

Organization 

NovaPay, a fictional Vietnamese fintech company, provides 1 electronic payment platform. 

System 

NovaPay Transaction Platform. 

Activity 

Quarterly access review. 

Review period 

Q2 2026. 

Accounts in scope 

Employee accounts, privileged accounts, and service accounts. 

Review scope 

Access rights, authorization, periodic review, access modification, revocation, and evidence retention. 

 

